><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>News from Google Team</name><title/><department/><company/></author></item><item><title>5 ways to host the ultimate dinner party with Google Search</title><link>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/search/dinner-party-hosting-tips/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Dinner_parties.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><media:description>An illustrated black magnifying glass with a sparkle in a white circle surrounded by a dinner party tablescape</media:description><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Dinner_parties.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;These AI features can help you craft a menu, design a tablescape, and handle other party-planning tasks.</description><pubDate>Tue, 28 Jul 2026 13:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/search/dinner-party-hosting-tips/</guid><category>Search</category><category>AI</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>5 ways to host the ultimate dinner party with Google Search</title><description>These AI features can help you craft a menu, design a tablescape, and handle other party-planning tasks.</description><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/search/dinner-party-hosting-tips/</url></og><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>News from Google Team</name><title/><department/><company/></author></item><item><title>3 Google updates from Galaxy Unpacked 2026</title><link>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/platforms/android/galaxy-unpacked-2026/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Unpacked_hero.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><media:description>Gentle Monster glasses, Warby Parker glasses, a prompt asking for the history behind a pictured building, and a prompt asking to book a table at a pictured restaurant</media:description><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Unpacked_hero.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;We shared how Samsung users can boost productivity and get time back on new foldables, watches, and glasses coming soon.</description><pubDate>Wed, 22 Jul 2026 13:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/platforms/android/galaxy-unpacked-2026/</guid><category>Gemini App</category><category>Android</category><category>Gemini Notebook</category><category>AI</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>3 Google updates from Galaxy Unpacked 2026</title><description>We shared how Samsung users can boost productivity and get time back on new foldables, watches, and glasses coming soon.</description><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/platforms/android/galaxy-unpacked-2026/</url></og><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>Menaka Shroff</name><title>VP of Android Ecosystem Marketing</title><department/><company/></author></item><item><title>Connect more of your apps to Search</title><link>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/search/connected-apps/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/ConnectedAppshero.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><media:description>Connected apps rendering</media:description><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/ConnectedAppshero.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;You’ll be able to securely link and interact with your go-to services directly in AI Mode.</description><pubDate>Thu, 16 Jul 2026 16:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/search/connected-apps/</guid><category>Search</category><category>AI</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>Connect more of your apps to Search</title><description>You’ll be able to securely link and interact with your go-to services directly in AI Mode.</description><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/search/connected-apps/</url></og><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>Chips Mistry</name><title>Senior Product Manager</title><department>Search</department><company/></author><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>Biharck Araújo</name><title>Engineering Lead</title><department>Search</department><company/></author></item><item><title>Create, edit and star in videos with two Google Vids updates</title><link>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/workspace/gemini-omni-personal-avatars/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/omni-blog-header_OarEe2t.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><media:description>Text "Gemini Omni and Personal Avatars in Google Vids" surrounded by various images</media:description><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/omni-blog-header_OarEe2t.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;Gemini Omni and personal avatars in Google Vids make video creation easier than ever.</description><pubDate>Thu, 16 Jul 2026 16:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/workspace/gemini-omni-personal-avatars/</guid><category>Google Workspace</category><category>Google One</category><category>AI</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>Create, edit and star in videos with two Google Vids updates</title><description>Gemini Omni and personal avatars in Google Vids make video creation easier than ever.</description><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/workspace/gemini-omni-personal-avatars/</url></og><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>Justin Luk</name><title>Product Manager</title><department/><company/></author></item><item><title>Celebrating 25 years of visual search innovation</title><link>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/search/google-images-25th-anniversary/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Google_Images_25th_hero.max-600x600.format-webp.webp" width="540"/><media:description>Google Images logo surrounded by illustrations of people searching for different images</media:description><description>&lt;img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/gweb-uniblog-publish-prod/images/Google_Images_25th_hero.max-600x600.format-webp.webp"&gt;Google Images is turning 25. Here’s a look back at some major milestones — and new ways to explore and create visual content.</description><pubDate>Tue, 14 Jul 2026 16:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/search/google-images-25th-anniversary/</guid><category>Search</category><category>AI</category><og xmlns:og="http://ogp.me/ns#"><type>article</type><title>Celebrating 25 years of visual search innovation</title><description>Google Images is turning 25. Here’s a look back at some major milestones — and new ways to explore and create visual content.</description><site_name>Google</site_name><url>https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/search/google-images-25th-anniversary/</url></og><author xmlns:author="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><name>Brad Kellett</name><title>Senior Engineering Director</title><department>Search</department><company/></author></item><item><title>Expanding Managed Agents in Gemini API:  background tasks, remote MCP and more</title><link>https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/developers-tools/expanding-managed-agents-gemini-api/</link><media:content height="540" medium="image" url=